			<div class="content" id="post-content-3862006">
									

<p>I was expecting more of a follow-up to this line, which I'm not sure ever really materialised:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>MOROZOV: In our line of work, Mr Erhardt, we are prone to believe things beyond comprehension hold fearful power. That we are helpless before them. But the most fearful powers are earthly.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I was expecting some big development following this, but the only thing that seemed to happen was the reveal that basically everyone is infected with this thing.</p>
<p>It's an interesting idea and well written, but I felt like not much really happened? The soviets developed a weapon, deployed it, and ultimately it's going to work as intended, just on everyone and on a longer time-table? I think maybe the punch of &quot;the Foundation is infected&quot; has been done just enough that it wasn't a particularly huge reveal to me.</p>

							</div>

								
					
